From 7444a9bf8c439f3dcffe429a431c39c591c919a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 17:32:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add cross-provider LLM fallback (e.g. Claude -> OpenAI on
 rate limit)

Adds an opt-in models[].fallback_models config so a run can keep going
through a rate limit, a billing issue, or bad credentials on one
provider by retrying the same request against another configured
model, in order, before giving up.

- ModelConfig.fallback_models: list[str] | None (config/model_config.py),
  excluded from the kwargs create_chat_model forwards to the provider
  client (models/factory.py), like pricing/context_window already are.
- LLMErrorHandlingMiddleware resolves the chain once at construction
  from the agent's configured model name (dropping unresolvable,
  duplicate, or self-referential entries with a warning) and, on
  primary-model exhaustion for a fallback-eligible reason (retry budget
  exhausted, or a quota/auth rejection), retries the same ModelRequest
  against each fallback in turn via request.override(model=...) before
  building the final user-facing failure message. Unclassified
  ("generic") errors are not eligible, so a real bug isn't masked by a
  provider swap. Behavior is unchanged when no model_name/fallback
  chain is configured.
- Threads model_name from build_middlewares (lead agent) and the
  subagent executor's already-resolved model name through
  build_lead_runtime_middlewares / build_subagent_runtime_middlewares /
  _build_runtime_middlewares so LLMErrorHandlingMiddleware knows which
  model's fallback_models to use.
- config.example.yaml + backend/docs/CONFIGURATION.md document the new
  field with a worked Claude Sonnet -> GPT-4 example; config_version
  bumped 45 -> 46.
- Tests: model_config field round-trip, factory exclusion regression,
  and dedicated sync/async fallback-chain coverage (dedupe/self-ref/
  unresolvable entries, success after primary exhaustion, quota-error
  fallback, chain-exhausted message, generic errors skip fallback,
  fallback-model construction failure is skipped not fatal). Existing
  suites updated only where they stub build_lead_runtime_middlewares /
  build_subagent_runtime_middlewares / LLMErrorHandlingMiddleware with
  a fixed keyword signature.
