+# ``_classify_error`` reasons that trip the circuit breaker on final exhaustion
+# (see the "record failure vs. release probe" branch in ``wrap_model_call`` /
+# ``awrap_model_call``). Quota/auth are configuration problems, not "provider
+# down", and burst_rate is a slope-throttle rather than an outage (issue
+# #4290) - none of those should fast-fail every other call for the recovery
+# window, so only a genuinely exhausted transient/busy failure counts.
+_CIRCUIT_TRIPPING_REASONS: frozenset[str] = frozenset({"transient", "busy"})
+
+# Reasons worth retrying against a configured fallback model (see
+# ``ModelConfig.fallback_models``): the primary's retry budget ran out
+# (transient/busy/burst_rate) or the account/credentials are the problem
+# (quota/auth) - both are exactly the cases a *different* provider can plausibly
+# route around. ``admission`` (our own local pacing, not a provider signal) and
+# ``generic`` (an unclassified error, possibly a real bug) are excluded:
+# swapping providers wouldn't address either and could mask the real cause.
+_FALLBACK_ELIGIBLE_REASONS: frozenset[str] = frozenset({"transient", "busy", "burst_rate", "quota", "auth"})
